\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Below is the cleaned final version, with the product model tightened, the journeys made more user-real, and the screen view updated to reflect the full system.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 Product structure\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 The app should be understood as five clear product areas rather than one long chain of actions: 
\f1\b Project Home
\f0\b0 , 
\f1\b Source and Segmentation
\f0\b0 , 
\f1\b Study Workspace
\f0\b0 , 
\f1\b Patching
\f0\b0 , and 
\f1\b Exams
\f0\b0 .\
Project Home is the stable return point for the whole app. Study Workspace is the stable shell for everything that happens inside one segment. Source and Segmentation is preparation and publishing, not part of the normal study loop. Patching is a controlled correction mode, separate from study. Exams is a focused assessment mode that still links back into normal remediation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 Core product rules\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 A 
\f1\b segment
\f0\b0  is the stable study unit: compiled source, tracker, anchors, and tree position. A 
\f1\b current record
\f0\b0  is the current authoritative saved outcome for that segment. One segment may have at most one current record at a time, but they are not the same object.\
A discussion session must always end with exactly one saved summary. Multiple summaries for the same segment are acceptable and desirable; multiple summaries for one session are not.\
Discussion summaries should always attach to 
\f2\fs26 segment_id
\f0\fs24 . When discussion happens after pass, they should also attach to 
\f2\fs26 current_record_id
\f0\fs24 . When discussion happens around a failed attempt, they should attach to 
\f2\fs26 attempt_id
\f0\fs24  instead.\
Pass should auto-save. There should be no separate mandatory save click after success.\
Skip for now is a navigation action, not authoritative study truth.\
Exams should be designed around progressive autosave. Engineering can implement this as debounced continuous save or lightweight checkpoints, but the product assumption should be that work is preserved as the user goes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

